<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Sept retail sales fall 2.6 percent on yr.</title>
<headline>Singapore Sept retail sales fall 2.6 percent on yr.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's September retail sales index (base 1991) fell 2.6 percent compared to a year ago, the Department of Statistics said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The index rose 4.2 percent from August 1996.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles, the index registered a month-on-month rise of 1.2 percent in September.</p>
<p>September retail sales were estimated at Singapore $1.97 billion. The statistics department said that year-on-year, in constant prices, the retail index fell by 1.5 percent.  </p>
<p>    Retail Sales Index (at Current Prices)   (pct change)</p>
<p>				   Month-on-Month     Yr-on-Yr</p>
